  "initialFindings": [
    "Private console allocation rollback rejected a not-yet-created transcript: reproduced on unchanged 0.79.4 kernel, fixed only transaction validation.",
    "Old heap comparison confused retained allocator capacity with live allocations; strict used-byte/block and error accounting retained.",
    "CLEANUPD expected 33 instead of 36 cases and one output payload per console instead of segmented/completion-owned output.",
    "Full storage fixture needs PROGRAMLIFECYCLE selftest=yes and SVCSTALL; first incomplete fixture runs were failures.",
    "GDB caught a page fault with physical owner rank30/depth1 during AVL mutation and a later self-link. Pure original AVL passed 20,000 seeded operations. Owner admission now prepares 64 KB of stack; faults under no-sleep/runtime owners are rejected before resolution. Actual moving-guard regression is case37.",
    "Warm-up retained exactly one 16424-byte child-output block in the parent transcript. The measured ASYNIOD /KILLWAIT fixture now uses /QUIET; all exact owner/byte/allocation comparisons remain.",
    "Mixed churn similarly retains CSTARTD success output in its parent. /QUIET preserves all C ABI/import/VM checks and error output; parent baseline printing moves after measurement. No exact accounting or cycle count is weakened."
  ],
  "reproduce": "Run-Qemu.ps1 and facade scripts are snapshots rooted at Temp/gfx-07905. Restore them there in this source revision. Private Test AUTOEXEC is restored byte-for-byte. Each run uses a fresh isolated 2048-MB image, SMP4 and natural poweroff.",
  "limitations": [
    "GPU-VA is driver-owned residency metadata; no NVIDIA PTE/VRAM backend or actual GPU DMA submission is implemented in this subversion.",
    "MMIO above 4 GB uses a fake-backend owner proof; EXAMPLE tests invalid real requests only.",
    "CPU software completion does not prove visible scanout or vblank.",
    "Builds and guest probes ran on Debian; Windows uses shared PowerShell logic but was not executed."
  ]
}
